The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
10\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{10}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{10} \cdot \dfrac{10}{10}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{10}
\end{align}$

The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
110\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{110}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{11}{10} \cdot \dfrac{10}{10}\\\\
&=\dfrac{11}{10}
\end{align}$
